# menu-vk.script — Q5 VK leg (task 44b): Dear ImGui Options menu end-to-end.
#
# Drives: open menu (Options button click) -> no-op click (deterministic
# resume checkpoint) -> FPS slider drag 16->32 (D4 uSecondsPerFrame path,
# applied per drag step like XmNvalueChangedCallback) -> Save -> drag away
# -> Load (round-trip restores 32) -> Mute on/off (toggle round-trip) ->
# Close (pause ends, simulation resumes at the new period).
#
# Geometry and assertions mirror the GL leg (menu-gl.script / task 44a)
# exactly: the seam class is engine-typed, so the same widget layout applies
# through the vkBackend adapter. Assertions live in qa/menu-vk-q5.sh (the
# driver): measured frame-period shift via live frame-counter sampling,
# pause via frozen state-hash/counter files, state-hash continuity (no
# reset/skip across the pause), and pixel identities between captures
# (compare -metric AE). Menu screens are backend-specific BY DESIGN
# (D9/F2) — no cross-backend reference diff.
#
# Geometry (deterministic: fixed ImGui window at (40,60) 430x190, canonical
# 688x702 client, identity letterbox):
#   Options button   (2,2)..(~62,32)          -> click (20,15)
#   FPS slider row   y 90..108, x 50..325     -> grab (150,99), release (132,99) = 32
#                                             -> release (90,99)  = ~20
#   Mute checkbox    (50,135)..(62,148)       -> click (56,141)
#   Save button      (50,158)..(80,175)       -> click (55,166)
#   Load button      (90,158)..(127,175)      -> click (108,166)
#   Close button     (137,158)..(178,175)     -> click (157,166)
#   dead space       inside window, no widget -> click (350,220)
#
# Run (via the driver, which also samples the counter/state-hash files):
#   qa/menu-vk-q5.sh
# Manual:
#   ./obj/harness --seed 12345 --script test/harness/scripts/menu-vk.script \
#       --out DIR --hiscore test/harness/fixtures/hiScore.nul.data \
#       --handshake frame --keep

1    capture title             # title/help screen; menu usable from here too

3    keydown s                 # start the game (16 fps baseline)
6    keyup s
40   capture start

# --- baseline pacing window (16 fps, ~62.5 ms/frame) -----------------------
90   capture pre_a
130  capture pre_b

# --- open the menu via the Options button (pause begins) -------------------
150  mousedown 20 15
154  mouseup 20 15
160  mousedown 350 220      # focus click: active title bar from here on
164  mouseup 350 220
170  capture menu_open

# --- no-op click in dead space: Q12-style checkpoint must not move ---------
200  mousedown 350 220
204  mouseup 350 220
240  move 350 220           # park the pointer: identical hover state
242  capture menu_noop

# --- FPS slider drag to 32 (each drag step applies through the D4 path) ----
260  mousedown 150 99
264  move 132 99
268  mouseup 132 99
296  move 350 220
300  capture menu_fps32

# --- Save preferences (writes the options.H-format file) -------------------
320  mousedown 55 166
324  mouseup 55 166
348  move 350 220
350  capture menu_saved

# --- drag away, then Load: round-trip must restore the saved state ---------
370  mousedown 150 99
374  move 90 99
378  mouseup 90 99
398  move 350 220
400  capture menu_dragged

420  mousedown 108 166
424  mouseup 108 166
458  move 350 220
460  capture menu_loaded

# --- volume/mute toggle round-trip -----------------------------------------
480  mousedown 56 141
484  mouseup 56 141
508  move 350 220
510  capture menu_muted

530  mousedown 56 141
534  mouseup 56 141
558  move 350 220
560  capture menu_unmuted

# --- close (pause ends; simulation resumes at the new period) --------------
580  mousedown 157 166
584  mouseup 157 166
620  capture menu_closed

# --- post window (32 fps, ~31.25 ms/frame) ---------------------------------
660  capture post_a
700  capture post_b
740  capture post_c

exit
